  "term": "sleep stages",
  "definition": "Sleep stages are distinct periods within sleep that are identified by patterns of brain-wave activity and related behavior. They are now commonly grouped as N1 and N2 for sleep onset and light sleep, N3 for slow-wave sleep, and REM sleep.",
